id: environment-shift
name: Environment Shift
uaType: magical
prerequisite: N/A
tpCost: 10
type: standard
actionCost: 1
kiCostPerBaseTier: 4
# The Quality and who stands in its Sphere asked when it is used (use-maneuver.mjs askShift); each of them marked with
# it until the start of your next turn - you only for Dangerous - and every other one offered the Movement Maneuver out
# of sequence for a Counter Action (chat.mjs postEnvironmentShift).
shiftsEnvironment: true
# Which Qualities it offers, and the one that reaches its user too: "You are unaffected by the effects of your chosen
# Environmental Quality (except Dangerous)". Named here, not in the code.
shiftQualities: aflame, bouncy, dangerous, electrified, frozen, poisonous
shiftAffectsSelf: dangerous
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The Squares of a Sphere around you Aflame, Bouncy, Dangerous, Electrified, Frozen or Poisonous until the start of your
  next turn - you unaffected but by Dangerous; anyone else inside may move away for a Counter Action.
text: >
  Environment Shift: You alter the world around you to suit your needs.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –TP Cost: 10
  –KP Cost: 4(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 1 Action
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: Target all Squares within a Sphere AoE (centered on you). Those Squares gain one of the following
  Environmental Qualities until the start of your next turn: Aflame, Bouncy, Dangerous, Electrified, Frozen, or Poisonous.
  You are unaffected by the effects of your chosen Environmental Quality (except Dangerous) until the start of your next
  turn.

  Any other Character who is within the Sphere AoE may spend a Counter Action to use the Movement Maneuver as an
  Out-of-Sequence Maneuver in response to this Unique Ability.
